WEBVTT

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:24.000
We're the ones who encouraged O-Tae to go
to rehearsals and perform in the shows...

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.590
Oh my god! Tamagawa's branches!

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:30.960
Yamabuki Bakery

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.140
Now's not the time to be getting upset...

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:42.210
We can get through this...

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.830
What can I do?

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.000
Asahi-san's guitar solo was so amazing!

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.920
Wasn't she looking for band members?

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.170
We should go talk to her!

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.680
Uh, I think she might be too good for us.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.080
Your performance yesterday
is creating quite the buzz, huh?

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.000
Lisa was totally in shock,
and I could hardly believe it either!

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.080
I hope PoPiPa are doing all right...

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.670
I can't bring myself to ask them about it.

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:06.500
I see O-Tae.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.830
O-Tae!

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.460
Morning!

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.040
Morning.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.670
Uh... Nice weather today.

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:22.510
I'm sorry... about the festival.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.210
I'm not mad at you...

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.330
I know you tried your best to make it.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.000
But...

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.460
you should apologize to Saaya.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.540
She was looking forward to it the most.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.040
I'm sorry.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:45.250
I said I'm not mad, okay?

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.380
Come on.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:50.790
Let's go!

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.000
Saaya.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.090
Morning!

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.330
Morning.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.670
Everything all right, O-Tae-chan?

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.390
I'm sorry about the culture festival.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.260
You don't have to apologize!

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:09.290
We bought lots of pastries 
from Saaya's place today.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.710
Let's all eat them together at lunch, okay?

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.080
Oh, you...

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.420
We were just worried about you.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:19.960
Thanks.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:24.960
Your family's chocolate cornets
really are the best, Saaya.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:27.790
Yamabuki Bakery never lets us down!

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.870
Do you think Rinko-senpai is here today?

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.160
I don't see why not.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.460
I want to apologize.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.460
Okay.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.420
We should all go thank 
her for helping us out!

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.040
I'll go myself.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:42.010
I'm the one who caused all the trouble.

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:44.970
We'll go together.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:45.880
Yeah!

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:49.000
She saved all of our butts, after all.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.460
Excuse us!

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.350
Huh? No one's here.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.290
Maybe she's in her classroom?

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.130
Where could she be?

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.460
Oh! There she is!

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.580
Wh-what is it?

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:06.330
Thanks from all of us.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:07.830
You shouldn't...

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:10.880
I should be apologizing for
not being able to buy enough time...

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:14.160
I'm really sorry I caused 
you all that trouble.

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:16.580
No, I should be sorry...

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:17.330
No, I'm sorry...

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.170
No, I'm sorry...

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.000
No, I'm sorry...

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:19.830
No, I'm sorry...

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:20.670
This could go on forever...
No, I'm sorry...

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:20.880
This could go on forever...

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:21.880
This could go on forever...
No, I'm sorry...

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:22.710
No, I'm sorry...

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.210
Thank you!

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:26.460
I'm sorry I-

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:27.580
It's fine!

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:31.130
My sister put on a great show,
and it all worked out in the end!

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.330
Yeah!

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:37.960
Aya-chan's MC was pretty horrific, though!

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.830
You're so mean, Hina-chan!

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:44.080
Rin-rin, they're about 17 minutes behind.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:45.250
All right.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:47.500
Um, everyone from Roselia...

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:49.420
What is it?

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:54.200
Thank you so much for covering for us
at the culture festival show last night.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.580
I'm really sorry I caused 
you all that trouble.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:02.750
It won't happen again.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.040
Okay!

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:06.290
Thanks again.

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.040
Interesting.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:12.670
I thought you'd be a lot harsher about it.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:15.130
I know why they were late.

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:18.060
I'm not just going to let it slide, but...

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:23.540
Do you remember that producer girl
who approached us a while back?

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.920
Oh yeah... she was short, right?

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:32.500
Her band, RAISE A SUILEN had their first
live show the same night as the festival.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:36.330
And Hanazono-san played 
support guitar for them.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:38.830
A self-sponsored show already?

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.040
What is it?

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:47.830
"...Their sound could soon make them
the new leaders of the girl band generation." Look!

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:50.130
Asahi Bathhouse

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.830
Thank you so much for helping us on stage.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.890
We owe you one, Lock!

00:06:56.890 --> 00:06:58.920
What? B-b-but I...

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.790
Your guitar solo was amazing!

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:02.210
Is that true?!

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:06.790
N-n-n-n-n-no way! PoPi-PoPi-Po... 
for y-you guys...

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:09.630
Lock!

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:10.380
Rokka-chan!
Lock!

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:11.080
Rokka-chan!

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.960
I'm glad we were able to 
say thank you to everyone.

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:20.210
So many people ended up helping us...

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.080
Wanna go to the warehouse?

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.500
You guys go on ahead.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:28.210
I need to make a stop somewhere.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:42.500
Yes! We're making waves!
More waves than I even predicted!

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:45.420
Congratulations! Congratulations!

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.500
Masking! Bake us a cake!

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.210
What kind of cake?

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:53.710
Hmm. The perfect cake for 
the greatest band ever...

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.540
Well, how 'bout strawberry!

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.160
Hana-chan.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.000
Congratulations!

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:04.210
You're on fire, Tae Hanazono!

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:06.920
People have been raving about you.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.590
I'm thinking of giving you
a guitar solo at our next show.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.590
We need to talk.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:16.640
Okay! I'm all ears!
Nothing could ruin the amazing mood I'm in!

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:24.770
I'd like to step down as 
support guitarist for RAS.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:31.990
Pardon?

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:35.500
I'd like to step down as support guitarist-

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:36.200
Why?

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:38.670
Hanazono, explain.

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:42.170
I didn't have the energy...

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:44.710
to do both, PoPiPa and RAS.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.170
Don't get me wrong, RAS's music is amazing.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:50.670
I wanted to learn how you create
your sound... to be like you.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:55.920
I thought that I could grow 
a lot here, with you...

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:03.080
I thought... if I could train with
such talented people, I-

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:04.040
Train?

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:05.940
Train, you say?!

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.330
This band is everything to me!

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:13.030
I don't need an amateur who just wants to
use this as a stepping stone!

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:13.670
That's not-

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:14.670
That's it, huh!

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:19.880
Quitting as soon as things get a little tough...
I didn't think you could be that selfish!

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:23.670
If you're gonna do something,
devote yourself to it 100%!

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.500
CHU2, can we have a minute?

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.080
Come back when you've cooled down.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:46.350
CHU2 knows you were serious about the band,
no matter what she says.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:50.000
Do you remember how insane
the cheers from the crowd were?

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:54.710
It's because they could feel
how passionate you were.

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:00.790
She's crazy for wanting to quit right now.

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:02.960
Our legend is just getting started!

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:05.620
She was only ever gonna be
a support member, though.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:11.000
It's still a shame... I was so happy when
Layer-san and Hana-san joined the band...

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.290
I guess.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:17.800
I was too naïve.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:24.670
I thought our self-sponsored show would fail
unless I did everything I possibly could. But...

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:29.290
Go back to Poppin' Party, Hana-chan.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.540
I'm sorry...

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:43.000
I told RAS that I would be 
leaving the band. Only...

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:48.420
they asked me to perform with them one last time,
at their next self-sponsored show...

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:53.340
Can I come and see you play?

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:54.130
What?

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:55.460
We should all go together!

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.300
I am a little curious.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:00.050
Count me in! How about you, Saaya-chan?

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:02.580
I'm in.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:19.380
Huh?

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:25.540
Here.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:28.630
Pareo's worried about you.

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:30.830
She thought you'd be crying out here.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.040
I'm not crying.

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:37.670
I made a promise to Hana-chan 
a long time ago...

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:51.920
Do you go to the music school?

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.250
Yep. Wanna sing?

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:55.330
No...

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:58.580
I don't sound like a kid when I sing.

00:11:58.580 --> 00:11:59.790
You don't?

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:02.080
Huh?

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:11.670
Here.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:33.290
You and Hana were in a band, huh?

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:34.790
No, actually.

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:35.710
What?

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.920
I had to move away for my parents' work...

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:48.830
Rei!

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:51.250
Hana-chan!

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:46.830
I saw her eyes tear up as we
sang together, and I knew...

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:49.290
knew I'd come back someday.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:53.640
Why don't you go stop her then?

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:56.960
I got to see her again...

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:58.750
That's enough.

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:05.920
No crying.

00:14:07.670 --> 00:14:09.210
I'm not crying.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:13.880
We're doing new costumes for
the self-sponsored show!

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:15.290
Ooh!

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:16.710
Oh...

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.790
Kinda plain, isn't it?

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.710
We could add things like this...

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.250
How 'bout this?

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.000
Ooh!

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:25.590
Nice.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:28.510
I want to add some kind of decoration!

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:29.580
How about a bow?

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:30.590
A bunch of bows!

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:32.080
How about right here?

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:32.880
Nice.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:33.880
Or here?

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:36.830
It's complete...

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:42.630
We can't use this.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:48.330
Stop!

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:53.500
Stay right there, Masking!

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:54.960
What?

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:56.750
You're going too crazy again.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.330
Ugh!

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.880
Only play what's absolutely 
necessary in this part.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.420
Simple is best!

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:06.170
Go for the ultimate sound...

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:08.550
'Kay.

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:10.090
Once more.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:20.670
Okay!

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:24.750
Tomorrow's live show is gonna become
the foundation for RAISE A SUILEN.

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.630
So buckle your seatbelts!

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:27.750
Yes!
Okay.

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:29.790
Tae Hanazono.

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:34.000
You're up last, so I'm gonna need you
to play me a home run!

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:34.880
I will!

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:38.210
I think the phrase is "hit" 
a home run, Mistress!

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:39.500
Whatever!

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:40.460
Once more...

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.080
Pareo!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.420
Stop it!

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:50.880
This is where Roselia played, huh.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:53.290
This is dub.

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:56.790
With a capacity of over 1,000,
plus amazing acoustics and atmosphere,

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:59.060
it's one of the best live venues in the city.

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.080
Maya-san!

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:01.130
Kasumi-san!

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:02.670
You're here too, Eve?!

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:04.790
Maya-san invited me!

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:07.920
This band has a super amazing drummer!

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:10.070
I didn't wanna come alone, though...

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:11.290
I'm just the wingman.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:13.630
They sponsored this so fast...

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:15.790
They haven't even been a 
band for that long, right?!

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:19.080
A lot of industry people 
keep their eyes on dub.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.710
Playing here is kind of a status symbol!

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.710
So many fans here already...

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.630
Not surprising, considering 
those two are in this band!

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:30.420
Huh?

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.860
The bass-vocalist, Rei-san and the drummer,

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:35.940
Masuki-san are actually a year younger than I am...

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:37.380
That means they're our age!

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:39.630
In any case, they're seriously good!

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:43.000
It's crazy they've only been
support musicians until now.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:45.000
Why not, if they're that good?

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:48.790
Rei's gotten tons of invites, but she's always
been devoted to her support work.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:51.790
I'm really surprised she 
joined RAS, actually...

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:55.170
As for Masuki? She's a mad dog.

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:56.380
A mad dog?

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:59.170
She always does a ton of crazy ad-libbing.

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:00.170
Ad-libbing?

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:02.830
It means she likes to improvise 
the beat on the spot.

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.580
If there's an opening,
she fills it with her crazy improv beats,

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:07.490
but sometimes she gets so crazy that no one can

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:09.840
keep up with her and it turns into a drum solo...

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:14.460
You can put her on a leash, but she'll still
lead the band where she wants to!

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:18.460
I mean, her pros outweigh her cons
in my eyes at least.

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:22.080
And by the sound of their music,
I'm guessing the other members are also pretty-

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:24.390
It's starting!

00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:26.020
Here they come!

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:34.210
On bass and vocals, Layer!

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:39.790
That's her! Rei Wakana!

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:42.490
They went to music school together!

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:47.670
On guitar, Hanazono!

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:49.080
Hanazono!

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:54.050
These fans are crazy...

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:56.880
On drums, Masking!

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:01.330
Yeah! King!

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:05.140
I can't believe I'm hearing Masuki-san live!

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:07.670
On keyboard, Pareo!

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:08.830
Pareo!

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:12.040
That girl comes to a lot 
of our meet and greets!

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:16.420
She even dyes her hair to match us
at different PasuPare events!

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:17.830
What? Are you serious?

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:24.170
We are RAISE A SUILEN!

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:30.170
Thank you! And...

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.000
Hanazono here.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:36.840
As we announced earlier,
today's the last day I'm playing as support.

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:37.920
Thank you!

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:39.130
Don't quit!

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.580
Come back!

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:41.830
Hanazono!

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:43.000
Thank you!

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:46.630
Our time together has been short,

00:20:46.630 --> 00:20:51.540
but I'll never forget these performances
or all of your amazing support!

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:53.960
Thank you so much!

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:55.540
Thank you!

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:57.710
Hanazono!

